    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a derived, read-only field computed purely from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, so I added it as a mapping expression rather than storing or computing it in any control-flow-heavy method.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   This yields e.g. `SMI-0007-M26` (year `2026` \u2192 `26`, zero-padded to two digits, matching the test's `registrationDate.substring(2,4)`).\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n- Only **two files** touched, and only **one function** materially changed (`toOwnerDto`, an annotation-only mapstruct interface method with CC = 1 and small `WMC_other` \u2014 the `OwnerMapper` interface has little surrounding complexity).\n- I avoided touching the large `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` method / controller class (huge `WMC_other`) and the many-method `Owner` entity. The value is derived at mapping time from fields already populated before serialization (`customerCode` set in the controller, `registrationDate` defaulted to non-null in its setter), so no new stored state or extra branching was needed.",
